5. Problem Solving:
   - Root cause fully confirmed and fixed: `computeRadarPoints` in `Radar.tsx` was adding an always-non-negative `angleBandSize` (derived from `getBandSizeOfAxis`, which returns `scale.bandwidth()` — always positive for d3 `scaleBand` regardless of range direction) to each point's raw `scale.map(name)` angle. Meanwhile, the rendered axis tick labels (`combineAxisTicks`) and tooltip-tick lookup (`combineTicksOfTooltipAxis`) both explicitly flip the sign of this same offset based on `mathSign(axisRange[0] - axisRange[1])` (positive/decreasing range → positive offset; negative/increasing range → negative offset). This meant that for the RadarChart's default decreasing range (`startAngle=90, endAngle=-270`), the signs happened to agree and the bug was invisible; for any increasing-range configuration (e.g. `startAngle=0, endAngle=360`, or various reversed/rotated variants), the drawn polygon's vertex angles ended up shifted by a full band-width in the wrong direction relative to the axis labels and tooltip resolution — reproducing both `mismatch.png` (shape vs. label mismatch) and `bug.png` (tooltip resolving to the wrong series) simultaneously, since all three symptoms trace to this single point-computation defect.
   - Fix implemented: compute `bandSizeSign = mathSign(range[0] - range[1])` (falling back to `1` if range is unavailable, preserving old default-direction behavior) inside `computeRadarPoints`, multiply it into `angleBandSize` before adding to the raw scale-mapped angle. The `range` value needed to reach `computeRadarPoints` was threaded through by adding a `range` field to the `AngleAxisForRadar` type and wiring `selectAngleAxisRangeWithReversed` into the `selectAngleAxisWithScaleAndViewport` selector's dependencies in `radarSelectors.ts`.
   - Verified fix correctness three ways: (a) direct numeric comparison of tick coordinates vs. radar point angles across 7 start/end angle configurations — all matched exactly (to floating-point precision) after the fix; (b) simulated mouse hover in jsdom for the previously-broken `0/360` configuration, confirming the tooltip now resolves to the correct series ("North", value 100) at the screen position where North's (corrected) tick/point coincide; (c) stash/pop test to prove the new regression tests genuinely fail without the fix and pass with it.
